# Repository attributes.
#
# .gitignore MERGE DRIVER — the fix for a conflict class, not a conflict
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lanes append their own ignore lines at the END of .gitignore, so with several
# branches open at once any two of them collide textually at EOF on a file
# whose contents are an unordered SET of rules. `merge=union` is git's built-in
# line-union driver: on a conflicting hunk it keeps the lines from BOTH sides
# instead of writing conflict markers, which is exactly right here — keeping
# both sides is always correct, dropping either is the one harmful outcome, and
# a duplicated rule is a no-op. Scoped to this ONE file: a structured file that
# collides on the same key with different values must be resolved by reading it.
.gitignore merge=union

# GENERATED, COMMITTED OUTPUT (rule 11 [R-DIST])
# -----------------------------------------------
# dist/ is Vite's build, committed so a Python-only desktop (D-5) always has a
# current build, and written on main only by .github/workflows/build-dist.yml.
# data/manifest.json is scripts/build_manifest.py's output, committed because
# GitHub Pages has no directory listing. linguist-generated keeps them
# out of language statistics and collapses them in reviews; -diff stops git
# from rendering a minified bundle as a text diff. Review by regenerating and
# comparing, never by reading the bytes.
dist/**            linguist-generated=true -diff
data/manifest.json linguist-generated=true

# Datasets: a CSV diff is never reviewable line by line (rule 12 [R-DATA] —
# append a file, never edit one in place).
*.csv -diff
